}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T06:53:21-08:00","id":63944,"title":"","content":"As good as anyone with a few extra dice to throw at the rolls. Their connection to Gaia isn't at all like that of the Genesis Lords, so they aren't going to be getting anything nearly that good. They're shapeshifters, and are far more likely to instill traits by way of their heart's blood than by use of Craft (Genesis). It's the price at being better at giving people mutations than the Solars are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T07:45:51-08:00","id":63972,"title":"","content":"Given that Genesis engineering is not a *thing* in 3e? It's questionable how good can you be at an activity that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> However, the long term sorcerous projects that can create new lifeforms is something that's happening in 3e. But that's sorcery. I have to ask- why would Lunars be supremely skilled at a very specific subset of sorcery? Like, since when an Alchemist cretaing life in his laboratory is something that sounds Lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T07:46:15-08:00","id":63974,"title":"","content":"Craft (Genesis) isn't going to be a thing in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:09:23-08:00","id":63991,"title":"","content":"I could see a Lunar achieving a synergy between magical science and their shapeshifting.<br /> For example my version of Raksi creates new lifeforms for the express purpose of adding them to her Heart's Blood library and it's yielded a few interesting results, she actually has Moonsilver fingernails thanks to an extended study of Furnace Rhinos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:30:10-08:00","id":64012,"title":"","content":"Grow stuff in your belly is obviously Kimbery stick so Lunar fans will probably be stuck with animal sex, again !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:13:14-08:00","id":64143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/63858-how-good-should-lunars-be-at-genesis-engineering?p=63974#post63974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft (Genesis) isn't going to be a thing in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me a Sad Panda-Totem Lunar...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:41:52-08:00","id":64162,"title":"","content":"Enough so that rutting around with the local fauna to create beastfolk is largely optional, but only with the appropriate investment.<br /> <br /> Because really, who doesn't want to make a munchkin feel like a goatfucker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T20:48:53-08:00","id":64551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/63858-how-good-should-lunars-be-at-genesis-engineering?p=64012#post64012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grow stuff in your belly is obviously Kimbery stick so Lunar fans will probably be stuck with animal sex, again !</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh. Or a void-tech womb alchemical.<br /> <br /> You don't need to be the main splat/yozi for the job to be great/second best at something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/404-walrusjones","name":"WalrusJones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T01:28:06-08:00","id":64676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/63858-how-good-should-lunars-be-at-genesis-engineering?p=64143#post64143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me a Sad Panda-Totem Lunar...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, apart from sorcerous projects to generate strange lifeforms, I doubt that it would be impossible to create Artifacts that generate lifeforms, or even lifeforms constructed as Artifacts, not to mention weird breeding program stuff.<br /> <br /> Just not as some weird tangential sub-craft that is also framed in a manner that is not entirely genre suitable.<br /> <br /> I mean, Craft (Magitech) probably also will not be a thing, but I don't think this means that people will be incapable of building things that Second Edition would have called magitech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T01:35:08-08:00","id":64678,"title":"","content":"As for the question, I can see a portrayal of the First Age that hints that a lot of new or artificial lifeforms were made by Lunar artifice. Not strictly because Lunars have Charms that make them better at it or that let them be living incubators (beyond the capacity of everything that has a womb to be an incubator), but more because a disproportionate number of Lunars pursue it since their mindset and experiences lean them in the direction of curiosity and creativity about strange new life forms.<br /> <br /> This might include Lunars who have them artificially inseminated with such life forms, possibly because it serves an exotic component requirement when they're Artifacts, or because they're pursuing the idea that being sustained in a Lunar body will make them stronger, or other reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T20:45:42-08:00","id":65365,"title":"","content":"Better than most anyone currently alive. See, if designing new forms of life is a sorcerous project, which is a cool idea that I like, it stands to reason that you are good at it by being an experienced sorcerer and by gaining access to bizarre sorcerous ingredients. The best sorcerers alive in the setting are Sidereals and Lunars.<br /> <br /> Sidereals don't have much reason to design new species. Sure, maybe inventing the Wolfbat so you can tell a homeless god &quot;you're the god of wolf bats now&quot; is a nice trick, but at the end of the day there's probably an easier way to accomplish your goal than introducing a new and untested variable to the balancing act that is already your job. Fundamentally, SIDS are servants of the status quo, and even the ones who want to change things don't want to change them by introducing sentient swarms of maneating bees.<br /> <br /> Lunars have the sorcerous power, the isolated fortresses, the outsider status and the combination of a victim complex and slight transhumanist hubris you need to make a really good Mad Scientist. Who else has as much incentive to design and create monster? Not only does a Lunar sorceress who creates a monster now have a monster she can direct towards the Realm, she probably adds directly to her personal power by adding a new shape to her repertoire.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, Dragonbloods are probably the next-best at this sort of thing. They've got schools of sorcery and the whole wealthy aristocrat who thinks his learning and birth makes him qualified to overrule nature thingy going on...again, lots of good mad science fodder here. Dynasts engineered mole hounds to hunt Dune People and hearth cats and I'd be surprised if they are not working on breeding dinosaur cavalry that's immune to fire or poison. The Realm has the resources to breed new species en masse, and a sorcerer who can find a need and design a beast to fill it has a strong economic and political and religious incentive to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 02-05-2014, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T00:13:28-08:00","id":65453,"title":"","content":"I do know that one thing I did was hack the necrotech rules for lunar biomonsters-- it's actually pretty easy, lose the decaying and needs repair defects and replace them with &quot;needs food&quot; and &quot;can be infected by diseases&quot; defect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T04:15:08-08:00","id":65548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/63858-how-good-should-lunars-be-at-genesis-engineering?p=63974#post63974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft (Genesis) isn't going to be a thing in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>And for that reason I therefore reject your canon and substitute my own <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T09:10:15-08:00","id":65737,"title":"","content":"Creating new forms of life and self-propagating species?<br /> <br /> Solars have the best potential. Followed by Infernals. Because of their Craft and Medicine Charms, and the most powerful forms of sorcery in the universe.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted are third, thanks to having Celestial Circle Sorcery and Heart's Blood shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Everyone else is worse. Sidereals and Abyssals have access to Celestial Circle Sorcery, but they don't have Heart's Blood shapeshifting. The Sidereal Charmset is limited, closed and finicky and the Abyssals kill stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T09:19:56-08:00","id":65745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/63858-how-good-should-lunars-be-at-genesis-engineering?p=65548#post65548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And for that reason I therefore reject your canon and substitute my own</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not in the 3E wiki, but I believe the Demented One said that the new sorcery system covers undertaking various sorcerous projects on top of casting spells. Creating life included. So the power is available, but it's not a Craft power","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/214-brontes","name":"Brontes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T09:35:08-08:00","id":65763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are probably the best at doing it very quickly within a narrow set of constraints because they can hybridize with anything they can fuck, but creating new weird shit is probably harder for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it! That's the thing I was thinking of; they've got some means that are incidentally capable of lending them a hand at the endeavor while detached from the usual necessary infrastructure, but not quite taking the form of personally substituting for said infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Making strange new life forms will probably be a thing some Lunars do, as an implementation of their wider goals, and as something that complements their own inherent methodology well, and they might be doing it more frequently than other groups because the necessary infrastructure doesn't widely exist anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T09:37:24-08:00","id":65766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/63858-how-good-should-lunars-be-at-genesis-engineering?p=63991#post63991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a Lunar achieving a synergy between magical science and their shapeshifting.<br /> For example my version of Raksi creates new lifeforms for the express purpose of adding them to her Heart's Blood library and it's yielded a few interesting results, she actually has Moonsilver fingernails thanks to an extended study of Furnace Rhinos.</div> </div> </div> </div>So stealing this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/999-winterstar","name":"Winterstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T12:31:33-08:00","id":65864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/63858-how-good-should-lunars-be-at-genesis-engineering?p=65737#post65737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating new forms of life and self-propagating species?<br /> <br /> Solars have the best potential. Followed by Infernals. Because of their Craft and Medicine Charms, and the most powerful forms of sorcery in the universe.<br /> <br /> Lunar Exalted are third, thanks to having Celestial Circle Sorcery and Heart's Blood shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> Everyone else is worse. Sidereals and Abyssals have access to Celestial Circle Sorcery, but they don't have Heart's Blood shapeshifting. The Sidereal Charmset is limited, closed and finicky and the Abyssals kill stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat.<br /> <br /> Mostly, the Lunar and Solar approaches to this topic are likely to differ a lot in scale, approach, ease-of-use and thematics, to the point where they're nearly two different concepts.<br /> <br /> If you want to dramatically alter the setting by creating a new rapidly self-propagating race according to your own (mostly) arbitrary specifications, that's probably a sorcerous working in 3e; and, either way, in any edition, that's the kind of thing that Solars (and their Infernal and Abyssal kin) are going to be better at, since they're the ones more focused on powers that kick over the table and break the world. (In 3e it is likely to be substantially harder, based on what we've heard -- it's not just activating a charm -- but the basic idea that Solars have that sort of setting-smashing potential is still core.) It's not exclusive to them, but they're going to have the best tools for approaching big 'rewrite the world' projects of that nature.<br /> <br /> If you want to produce more specific sorts of strange creatures under your thematics (like beastmen), or perhaps birth individual monsters from your own womb or something, Lunars can do that much more easily than a Solar can accomplish a big sorcerous working, but those will be specific powers tied to a specific thematic. Lunars aren't going to be generic masters of creating new races any way they please, but they could be masters of birthing a race of monsters from their own bodies (or having it boil forth from their flesh like gremlins or something.)<br /> <br /> In general, the thematic distinction is going to be that Lunars are good at birthing beastmen and monsters through their own inherent traits; but Solars are going to be much better at doing it using talent, knowledge and skill, or vast sorcerous workings or approaches of that nature.<br /> <br /> (Also, words are important. Genetic engineering is mostly not a thing in Creation. But if you want someone who is good at putting bits of living things in vats and growing them into new monsters using magic, a Twilight will be your best bet, although obviously a Lunar Sorcerer will by no means be incompetent; if you want to play Echidna, Mother of Monsters, you will be better off playing a Lunar.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-05-2014, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T12:49:25-08:00","id":65879,"title":"","content":"Lunars can perform a lot of breeding shenanigans by getting involved, uhm. Personally.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, creating life is the work of sorcerers, and is something you approach as a sorcerer rather than as X Y or Z brand of Exalt, generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}